            <ArticleTitle>Chronic Compartment Syndrome of the Mobile Wad: A Case Report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>516-518</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1142/S0218810417720364</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of chronic compartment syndrome of the mobile wad in a 15-year-old female amateur tennis player is described. She presented with a 7-month history of radial forearm pain and tenderness with mild swelling, and was unable to swing the tennis racket. MRI showed high intensity within the brachioradialis muscle. Endoscopic fasciotomy showed degeneration of the brachioradialis muscle belly. Complete pain relief was obtained 4 months after the fasciotomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
